{{smaller block|The flat, levell, and plaine fields not able to afford us . . . any ''borough'' to shelter us.
{{right|''Holland'', tr. of Ammianus, p. 114.}}}}
'''5†.''' At Richmond in Yorkshire, England, and perhaps other northern old corporate towns, a property held by burgage, and formerly qualifying for a vote for members of Parliament. ''N. E. D.''—'''Close borough,''' {{smaller|a pocket borough.}}
